# walking — a way the party knows is walked on the map for nothing, and a new way back teaches
#
# There is no act of going back. Ground already stood on is reached by a click on its card, by ways
# already gone by: no thought, no roll, no point. The plain way to such ground is no longer a symbol
# on the card either — its line is on the map.
#
# A way NOT yet gone by is still an act. When it comes out on ground already stood on, what the walk
# teaches is how the place joins up (Verb.WayBackLessons): the Field–Rock Track, found at the rock
# after the field and the yard were both walked, teaches Retracing rather than the track's own
# lesson.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# Field -> yard, by an act: the way is not known yet.
strategy succeed
goal move
click observe "Test Yard"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "Test Yard"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect Moved to: Test Yard
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-state where Test Yard

# From the yard the field is ground stood on: no symbol for the way to it, and the card walks there.
expect-no-state symbols "the way to Test Field"
expect-state noetic points=3/3
click area "Test Field"
wait
expect-state where Test Field
expect-state noetic points=3/3
expect-state map walk from Test Yard to Test Field
click area "Test Yard"
wait
expect-state where Test Yard

# Yard -> rock, by an act again.
click observe "Test Rock"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "Test Rock"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect Moved to: Test Rock
click continue
advance 12 180

# At the rock, the track to the field is a way never gone by that comes out on known ground.
goal follow_path
click observe "Field–Rock Track"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "Field–Rock Track"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect Moved to: Test Field
expect-verb follow_path
expect Modus mentis learned: Retracing
click continue
advance 12 180

# The track is known now, and walked back for nothing.
click area "Test Rock"
wait
expect-state where Test Rock
quit
